{"componentChunkName":"component---src-templates-template-book-js","path":"/books/calendar/","result":{"data":{"site":{"siteMetadata":{"url":"https://poetry.me.uk"}},"markdownRemark":{"html":"<p>A Year in Verse: Celebrating the Western Spirit</p>\n<p>Step into a lyrical journey through the Western calendar with this rich collection of metered, rhyming poetry. A Year in Verse brings to life the spirit of the seasons, marking the dates and events that have shaped Western culture with wit, warmth, and poetic precision.</p>\n<p>From the icy glow of Christmas to the budding promise of May Day, from the sun-drenched magic of Mid-Summer’s Day to the eerie shadows of Halloween, the year is punctuated by four sweeping narrative poems—each one a vivid tribute to the festivals that divide and define our time.</p>\n<p>Interwoven between these cornerstones are finely crafted poems that reflect on historical milestones, cultural traditions, and the quiet, often overlooked beauty of the calendar's rhythm.</p>\n<p>Years in the making, this collection is the result of long dedication, recently reignited by fresh inspiration. It is a heartfelt homage to the myth, memory, and meaning that shape the Western world.</p>\n<p>This is poetry for those who feel the turning of the year in their bones—and celebrate it in their hearts.</p>","excerpt":"A Year in Verse: Celebrating the Western Spirit Step into a lyrical journey through the Western calendar with this rich collection of metered, rhyming poetry. A Year in Verse brings to life the spirit of the seasons, marking the dates and events that…","fields":{"slug":"/books/calendar/"},"frontmatter":{"date":"September 06, 2022","title":"Calendar","tags":"poetry poems book UK English England Culture Tradition Calendar Occasions Festival","download":"/download/calendar","preview1":{"childImageSharp":{"fluid":{"base64":"data:image/png;base64,","aspectRatio":0.5617977528089888,"src":"/static/0058c95438410cb6d08093c127c29e1a/3c17d/calendar_poetry_co